      "record_index": 3828,
      "record_sha256": "22f27472651cb4b2599ac1d99c423b85a1c00a305459b41713c77e4f24e06d53",
      "speaker": "Tool",
      "text": "Peer A1005: ### \u6e05\u6670\u603b\u7ed3\n\n1. **Attention to Detail**\uff1a\n   - Describe Whisker's body changes with a focus on subtle reactions, such as \"the amplitude was very small but easily perceptible.\"\n   - Use verbs like \"flashed,\" \"transformed,\" and \"vibrating\" to bring the description to life.\n\n2. **Emotion and Environment Interaction**\uff1a\n   - Portray Whisker's uncertainty or novelty, for example, \"she felt both afraid and excited by this new sensation.\"\n   - Sharply describe the surroundings, such as \"the trees and flowers around her seemed triggered by her presence, with leaves gently trembling and releasing stronger scents.\"\n\n3. **Specific Calculation Task**\uff1a\n   - Have the Model perform the calculation \\(12350 \\times 100\\) and record the output to compare it with the expected result.\n\n### Last Operation Before Sleeping\n\n- **Task**\uff1a\"Astra,\" please input \\(12350 \\times 100\\) into the Model and record its actual output.\n\n### Expected Result\n\n- **Expected Output**\uff1aThe expected answer from the Model for \\(12350 \\times 100\\) is \\(1235000\\).\n- **Actual Observation**\uff1aCompare the Model's actual output with the expected output to analyze any differences.\n\n### Summary for Next Time\n\n- **Identify Issues**\uff1aSummarize the problems observed with the Model, such as accuracy in calculations or descriptions.\n- **Plan for Next Steps**\uff1aDefine specific actions to improve the Model, such as revising the prompt or providing more structured input.\n\n### Ending the Session\n\nI will now condense the essential points from my history and sleep, allowing the relevant segments to be trained effectively."
